{
  "opening": "This release introduces several new functions and improvements to existing ones, while also dropping support for Python 2. The public API will be expanded with new utilities for composition, inspection, and dictionary operations, alongside performance enhancements.",
  "requirements": [
    {
      "id": "m02",
      "text": "The `compose_left` function must be exposed as a public API entry point. It should accept an iterable of functions and return a new function that applies them from left to right."
    },
    {
      "id": "m03",
      "text": "The `peekn` function must be exposed as a public API entry point. It should take an iterable and a count, yielding the first n items while passing them through unchanged."
    },
    {
      "id": "m04",
      "text": "The `dissoc` function must remain available in the public API. It should remove specified keys from a mapping and return the resulting mapping without modifying the original."
    },
    {
      "id": "m05",
      "text": "The `Compose` class must be exposed as a public API entry point. It should allow users to create composed functions by providing a sequence of callables."
    },
    {
      "id": "m07",
      "text": "The `fold` function must continue to support parallel execution via multiprocessing. It should aggregate items from an iterable using a specified function, optionally distributing work across processes."
    },
    {
      "id": "m14",
      "text": "The `merge` and `merge_with` functions must accept any object implementing the Mapping interface, not just dictionaries. They should combine multiple mappings into a single result based on the provided strategy."
    },
    {
      "id": "m18",
      "text": "All listed public names must no longer support Python 2 syntax or runtime features. Functions like `curry`, `groupby`, and `merge_with` must operate exclusively under Python 3 semantics."
    },
    {
      "id": "m28",
      "text": "The library must provide signature compatibility for Python 3.10's `anext` built-in behavior where applicable. No new public names are required for this change, but internal signatures must align with 3.10 standards."
    }
  ],
  "closing": "Please ensure all new functions are properly documented and integrated into the main package namespace. Verify that Python 2 specific code paths have been completely removed."
}
